      "title": "Q7 \u00b7 Instrument self-check (if this fails, every panel above is void)",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "The metric's own HELP asserts these reconcile: decision=spend is ONE API request each, so sum(rate(scan_budget_decisions_total{decision=\"spend\"})) must track sum(rate(api_requests_total)) for the matching endpoint. If they diverge persistently the instrument is lying and every other panel on this dashboard is void. READ THE CUMULATIVE STAT TO THE RIGHT BEFORE RAISING AN ALARM: at these low absolute counts (~0.3-0.6 req/s) a short rate window jitters by 20%+ between the two counters purely from scrape alignment. Sustained one-directional drift is the real signal. api_requests_total carries NO player_id label - do not add $player to those two targets, it would return empty. Verified against /metrics.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "decimals": 4,
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*endpoint.*"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    10
                  ],
                  "fill": "dash"
                }
              }
            ]
